Q & A on sending events

Q:
The method which is mentioned in the manual (Section 11.4)
is for sending events between the windows under one LIspView
as follows:


                       +--------+
                       |LispView|
                       +---+----+
            +--------------+----------------+
            |                               |
        +-------+     lv:send-event     +-------+
        | Window|     ------------->    | Window|
        +-------+                       +-------+

   I`d like to know about how to send the events under the 
   following configuration.


	   +--------+                      +--------+
	   |LispView|                      |LispView|
	   +---+----+                      +---+----+
	       |                               |
	   +---+---+       send event      +---+---+
	   | Window|     ------------->    | Window|
	   +-------+                       +-------+


   I guess I can do that by using Xlib interface with the
   Foreign Function Interface.

A:

That's correct - you'll have to use X11:XSendEvent to do this.  The code
below illustrates roughly how you'd write this kind of thing.

(in-package "LISPVIEW")

(let* ((display-xid (xview-object-xid (device (display window))))
       (window-xid (xview-object-xid (device window)))
       (data (X11:make-bsl-union))
       (event 
	 (X11:make-XEvent
	   :type X11:ClientMessage
	   :display display-xid
	   :window window-xid
	   :message-type (x11-intern-atom display-xid 'your-message-type)
	   :format 32
	   :data data)))
  ;; init data
  (X11:XSendEvent display-xid window-xid X11:True 0 event)
  (X11:XFlush display-xid))

